          "title": "Rendering",
          "target": {
            "frame": "tile",
            "label": "Current slide"
          },
          "text": "The tab loads deck.html in a sandboxed iframe, like canvas frames. The canvas frame bridge then gives labels, pins, spotlight and history snapshots without new plumbing.",
          "x": -700,
          "y": 340,
          "w": 560
        },
        {
          "id": "n-tile-question",
          "kind": "design",
          "title": "Questions belong to a slide",
          "target": {
            "frame": "tile",
            "label": "Slide question"
          },
          "text": "The agent attaches a question to a slide. Picking an option queues it in the same answer queue as canvas and redline.",
          "x": -700,
          "y": 560,
          "w": 560
        },
        {
          "id": "n-tile-round",
          "kind": "design",
          "title": "Rounds",
          "target": {
            "frame": "grid",
            "label": "Slide 5 card"
          },
          "text": "Each Send makes a snapshot, as canvas does. Slides changed since the last round get a green badge and a diff toggle.",
          "x": 2640,
          "y": 120,
          "w": 420
        },
        {
          "id": "n-grid-reorder",
          "kind": "development",
          "title": "Reorder",
          "target": {
            "frame": "grid",
            "label": "Dragged slide"
          },
          "text": "Dragging writes the new order to deck.html and sends a note, the same way canvas layout drags work.",
          "x": 2640,
          "y": 400,
          "w": 420
        },
        {
          "id": "n-theme",
          "kind": "design",
          "title": "Themes are token files",
          "target": {
            "frame": "theme",
            "label": "Match a brand"
          },
          "text": "A theme is a ~25-line CSS file of tokens. Match a brand sends the source to the agent, which writes a new theme file and checks contrast.",
          "x": -700,
          "y": 1360,
          "w": 560
        },
        {
          "id": "n-pptx",
          "kind": "important",
          "title": "PPTX trade-off",
          "target": {
            "frame": "export",
            "label": "Export PowerPoint"
          },
          "items": [
            "v1 as one picture per slide + notes: looks identical, but text can't be edited in PowerPoint.",
            "Editable PPTX means rebuilding every layout with native shapes."
          ],
          "x": 2640,
          "y": 1120,
          "w": 420
